 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "Level 4 (inferred): InMemoryDB() starts empty; records hold string fields with string values. Every method takes a timestamp; timestamps across all calls are strictly increasing. setDataAt(key, field, value, timestamp) stores a value that never expires. setDataAtWithTtl(key, field, value, timestamp, ttl) stores a value that is live at times t with timestamp <= t < timestamp + ttl. Setting a field replaces its value and expiry. getDataAt(key, field, timestamp) returns the live value or \"\". deleteDataAt(key, field, timestamp) removes a live field and returns true, otherwise false. scanDataAt(key, timestamp) and scanDataByPrefixAt(key, prefix, timestamp) return the live fields of the record as \"field(value)\" strings ordered by field name, all of them or only those whose field starts with prefix. backup(timestamp) saves a copy of all fields live at timestamp together with their remaining lifetimes (expiry minus timestamp; no expiry stays no expiry) and returns the number of records that have at least one live field. restore(timestamp, timestampToRestore) replaces the whole database with the latest backup taken at or before timestampToRestore; a restored field with remaining lifetime r expires at timestamp + r. At least one backup taken at or before timestampToRestore always exists, and timestampToRestore < timestamp. Backups stay available after a restore. Every method call is answered in call order on one instance; void methods return nothing.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
    "path": "projects/algorithm_solver/catalogue/authored/hack2hire-chunk15-b-20261028-v1/contracts.json",
